  {
    "sha": "dfc87f09ea92aa8663e44a036ea53ddbbff02e55",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoKkgNoAKGRmYzg3ZjA5ZWE5MmFhODY2M2U0NGEwMzZlYTUzZGRiYmZmMDJlNTU",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "tbrasselle",
        "email": "tbrasselle@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-11T13:29:54Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "tbrasselle",
        "email": "tbrasselle@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-11T13:29:54Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(ui,app): the origin names get a persisted on/off switch (#645)\n\nThe rework ask on this PR: the #727 gizmo names answer to a toggle now,\ndefault on, persisted across restarts, with a structural test covering\nboth states.\n\n- `State.show_gizmo_names` (default on, the #727 decision) beside\n  `show_world_axes`; the browser pane grows a \"Show origin names\"\n  checkbox under \"Show world origin axes\". The flip is view state like\n  every other toggle - local copy, `.changed()`, written through\n  `set_gizmo_names` - never a command, never on the history - and the\n  choice goes out to disk at once.\n- `interact::overlay_labels` gates only the name rows: the triad lines\n  and the X/Y/Z letters never depend on the switch. New law test\n  `the_name_switch_quiets_names_not_letters_or_lines` pins exactly that;\n  the existing #727 count tests keep passing with the flag on.\n- Persistence: no view preference persists today - the only per-user\n  file is the recents one - so this adds `app::view`: a sibling\n  `view.json` (format `camcraft-view/1`) in the same config folder,\n  built on `recent::config_dir_for` and `machine::store::write_atomic`\n  like `recent` itself. Unknown-key tolerant, atomic write, creates\n  missing folders. `State::load_view` reads it in `Shell::new` right\n  after the recents; `state_view.rs` is the state-side wiring, mirroring\n  `state_recent.rs`. The decision - and the option of folding the file\n  into recent.json if the maintainer prefers - is recorded in\n  docs/decisions/727-viewport-gizmo-labels.md.\n- Tests: app `tests/view_prefs.rs` - round-trip, corrupt file starts\n  with names on, unknown keys ride through a rewrite, the store writes\n  where `CAMCRAFT_CONFIG_DIR` points; ui `egui_app::tests::view_names` -\n  real checkbox clicks both ways queue nothing, the file follows the\n  click, and a fresh shell over the same file keeps the choice;\n  structural gains the checkbox label in the live view-toggle list.\n- Pins: the new checkbox row moves the painted tree down one row\n  (+21.0 = row height + item spacing), so the hardcoded browser-pane\n  tree tops in tests.rs and tests/program_entry.rs move 200.0 -> 221.0,\n  the same move 30479ed7 made (179.0 -> 200.0) for the Projection row.\n  Pixel snapshots untouched: the release lane owns the PNGs (#255).\n\nGates: ui lib 448 passed / 0 failed (5 ignored), app suite green,\n`cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`\nclean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>",
      "tree": {
        "sha": "4c5f93672020d29ac95eb81a85b820ee85494db4",
